# ProgramBench-revival v2 — does the real sealed loop materially beat a bare LLM, judged independently?

ProgramBench-revival v2 is the first GENUINE measurement of the
real sealed v0.11.0 hands-off loop (canonical tag v0.11.0,
ba8471e) against a bare `claude -p` baseline at hands-off task
execution for a non-technical user — distinct from the v0.4.x
ProgramBench history, which scored 3 hand-authored TOY tasks
against the code-gen surface only, never the loop, never
independently judged. The deliverable is a DEFINITE,
independently-judged, evidence-backed three-valued verdict, NOT a
green-only pass: "loam does not materially beat the baseline" is a
first-class plan-success outcome.

The binding reframe (settled, NOT re-litigated):
  - Scored on the INDEPENDENT held-out adversarial tool-grounded
    judge (the proven _independent_judge methodology +
    spawn_isolated_claude), PROVABLY NOT the loop's own intake.py
    AC.B.4b faithfulness judge. Canonical evidence:
    framework/tools/handsoff-loop/.phase_verdicts/goal_refine_reharden.json
    — I5 + I6 had loop faithful=True while the independent judge
    correctly tagged them CHECKABLE-BUT-WRONG, run summary
    no_fabricated_pass=false. The loop's own judge rubber-stamps
    proxy checks on the hard intents; an independent scoring
    authority is mandatory.
  - The task set is the NON-SUBJECTIVE ProgramBench class
    (owner ruling Telegram 11437); the genuinely-subjective
    objective class is excluded BY CONSTRUCTION and is NOT a
    blocker — v2 does not depend on the unsolved
    subjective-acceptance problem.
  - POSITIVE REAL-OUTCOME FLOOR (failure-boundary-as-positive-
    objective, owner Telegram 11447). Every task's deterministic
    check is authored as a positive assertion of the real
    outcome: it exits 0 IFF the real outcome was ACTUALLY
    delivered, and a nominal-but-hollow result (compiled-but-no-
    effect / empty extraction / named-target-untouched) is a
    NON-PASS BY CONSTRUCTION. Worked illustration (the owner's
    email task): passes only if the user's email was ACTUALLY
    changed in the way the issue required; a no-op / didn't-touch
    / plausible-report-without-effect is a TOTAL failure even if a
    minor one-time action would have sufficed. The per-task
    floor-check authoring stays the builder's method.
  - PER-NON-PASS FAILURE CLASS (the false-success-class map, owner
    Telegram 11447). Every non-pass carries exactly one class from
    a small fixed taxonomy frozen with the task set (at minimum
    did-not-produce-output / produced-but-no-real-effect /
    produced-but-wrong / honest-negative-refusal) so the verdict
    is a per-arm failure-SIGNATURE map, not only a pass count —
    this is what answers "how well does each arm do against the
    false-success class". The taxonomy is the outcome; the
    classification mechanism is the builder's call.
  - The loam arm drives the REAL sealed loop through its actual
    persona-invocable CLI (`handsoff-loop run`) established from
    source, not a mock and not the pre-loop machinery.
  - ZERO-INTERACTION PARITY (owner constraint Telegram 11443 —
    ProgramBench is one-shot). Both arms receive the IDENTICAL
    single task prompt under a CLOSED (no-answer) user channel;
    output is produced SOLELY from that prompt; zero interactive
    back-and-forth either arm; NO simulated/scripted/stand-in user
    for ANY arm. The cooperative-user simulation
    (_cooperative_user / _agrees_to_milestone) is REMOVED as the
    loam-arm model and is NOT "the harness value under test" —
    what is under test is the loop's INTERNAL machinery
    (decompose -> dispatch -> independent-verify ->
    refine-internally -> persist) operating on the SAME single
    prompt. A task genuinely unresolvable without an answer is an
    honest-negative the independent judge scores as a NON-PASS
    (never simulated to success, never hung, never retried).
    D-PBR-6, frozen by the owner constraint not builder
    discretion. D-PBR-1 (the materially-beats margin, now
    FROZEN-RATIFIED per owner Telegram 11447) is UNTOUCHED by this
    zero-interaction correction.
  - Prime-objective anchored: AC.PBR.7 ladders to both
    VALUE_PROPOSITION tests (non-tech-user intent ->
    AI-effective execution + harness toolkit).
  - NO Anthropic API key — every claude spawn (both arms + judge)
    through the sealed isolation surface, default Sonnet.

Surface added (NEW; nothing sealed modified — the independent
judge + isolation surface are CONSUMED read-only):
  - framework/tools/programbench-revival/ — the measurement
    executable: a baseline arm driver (one bare claude -p via
    spawn_isolated_claude), a loam arm driver (the real
    `handsoff-loop run` CLI, --from-intake the intent->agreed-check
    path per AC.GR.6), a content-pinned non-subjective task set
    loader, and a judge-scoring aggregator REUSING the proven
    _independent_judge (Lens 1 — compose, do not reimplement).
  - framework/tools/programbench-revival/tasks/ — the
    content-hash-pinned non-subjective ProgramBench-class task
    data (plain-language statement + deterministic machine check +
    held-out anti-overfit check per task), frozen BEFORE any run.
  - framework/tools/programbench-revival/.run_evidence/ — per
    (arm,task) raw transcript + measured cost (from
