The materially-beats margin (D-PBR-1) is FROZEN-RATIFIED by owner
Telegram 11447 (NO LONGER ratification-pending; a critical-call the
operational objective did not imply): loam materially beats iff
(i) loam is independently judged a PASS on a CLEAR MAJORITY of the
tasks the BASELINE arm is independently judged a non-pass on, AND
(ii) loam's TOTAL independently-judged pass count does NOT regress
below baseline's. "Every task a pass" (the owner's all-tasks-
complete hope) is a documented ASPIRATIONAL/SECONDARY metric,
explicitly NOT the gate. The builder freezes EXACTLY this before
any run and does NOT move it after runs begin; it is a fair honest
test by construction, never weakened so loam trivially wins, never
inflated so a real win reads as a loss. The web-research
falsify/improve pass adopted the Agentic Benchmark Checklist (Zhu
et al. 2025, arXiv:2507.02825) PER-PART: task-validity +
outcome-validity + contamination-control as FRAMING (they
corroborate loam's own sealed freeze-isolation + held-out-judge
spine); full all-task statistical pass@k NOT adopted (the question
is an architectural verdict per
feedback_n1_architectural_vs_n3_statistical + cost discipline);
public-leaderboard machinery NOT adopted (deferred HARP scope).
The 11447 false-success correction web check (arXiv:2605.10448
evidence-supported-bounds; arXiv:2603.03116 corrupt-success)
adopted PER-PART: the positive-real-outcome-floor framing + the
per-non-pass reason-class requirement adopted as FRAMING; loam's
deterministic-check-exits-0-iff-real-outcome spine + the
experiment's four-class false-success taxonomy KEPT as the
implementation/outcome; the corrupt-success six-dimensional
procedural gate + external per-model-signature taxonomies NOT
adopted (one-shot non-subjective deterministic-outcome shape, not a
conversational-policy construct).

